The Problem: You have a massive, highly complex system made of dozens of different classes.
Imagine a user clicks "Buy Now" on Amazon. Behind the scenes, the server has to:

    Check the Inventory Database.

    Charge the Credit Card via the Payment Gateway.

    Generate a Shipping Label.

    Send an Email Receipt.

If you put all of this logic directly into your Web Controller or your UI button, your code becomes incredibly fragile.
The UI developer now has to understand exactly how 4 different backend systems work and call them in the exact perfect
order.

The Solution: You build a Facade (a French word meaning the "front face" of a building).
Think of it like the Front Desk at a hotel. You don't go to the basement to turn on the boiler, and you don't go to the
kitchen to cook your breakfast. You just call the Front Desk and say, "Room service, please," and they coordinate the
chaos for you.